  "packageName": "@workflow-builder/mcp-server",
  "readme": [
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "# @workflow-builder/mcp-server\n\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`wb-docs`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ": a stdio MCP server that serves the hand-written Workflow Builder docs ("
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`apps/docs/src/content/docs`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "), the READMEs of the published packages and the public TypeScript API of "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`@workflowbuilder/sdk`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`@workflowbuilder/ui`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " and "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`@workflowbuilder/temporal`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ". Private, not published.\n\n## Tools\n\n| Tool             | Use                                                                                                 |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`search_docs`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "    | Keyword search over documentation sections. Results carry an id, section title, URL and markdown.   |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`get_doc`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "        | Read a page or one section by id, or by an internal doc link such as "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`/get-started/theming/`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ".       |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`search_symbols`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " | Search exports and their members. Filters: "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`package`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " ("
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`sdk`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`ui`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`temporal`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ") and "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`kind`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ".          |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`get_symbol`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "     | Signature, JSDoc, members and a ready import statement for "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`sdk:Name`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`sdk:Name.member`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " or a name. |\n\nResponses are compact JSON in a single text item. Errors use "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`isError: true`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " with "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`{\"error\": \"...\"}`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ".\n\n## Build and run\n\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm --filter mcp-server build   # tsc + TypeDoc for the three packages, about 30 s\npnpm --filter mcp-server test    # unit tests, fixtures only, no build needed\npnpm --filter mcp-server smoke   # real corpus, needs a build\n```"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "\n\nThe repo-root "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`.mcp.json`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " registers the server as "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`wb-docs`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " ("
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`node packages/mcp-server/dist/index.js`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "). Claude Code loads MCP servers at session start, so build first and restart the session after rebuilding.\n\nDocs are read from "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`apps/docs/src/content/docs`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " and indexed in memory every time the server starts, so they are always current. Symbols come from "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`dist/data/typedoc/*.json`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", so they are as fresh as the last "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`build`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " (or "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`pnpm --filter mcp-server typedoc`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "). The server logs one line to stderr when it is ready.\n\n## Layout\n\n| Path                | Contents                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`src/config/`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "       | The tunable surface: ranking, synonyms, chunking, response budgets. Plain data, no logic.                                  |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`src/docs/`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "         | Page and README loading, MDX cleaning, chunking, ids and the docs search engine.                                           |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`src/symbols/`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "      | TypeDoc extraction, the type printer and the symbol search engine.                                                         |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`src/corpus/`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "       | "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`buildCorpus()`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ": the one entry point shared by the server and the smoke test.                                    |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`src/tools/`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "        | One folder per tool: "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`tool.config.ts`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " (schema and description), validator, handler.                                        |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`src/__fixtures__/`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " | Small checked-in docs and TypeDoc JSON used by the tests. "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`pnpm --filter mcp-server fixtures:update`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " regenerates the JSON. |\n| "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`scripts/`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "          | "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`generate-typedoc.ts`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " (build step), "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`smoke.ts`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`update-fixtures.ts`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ".                                                      |\n\n## Notes\n\n- Ids: pages are "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`guides/configuring-the-editor`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", sections "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`guides/configuring-the-editor#props-reference`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", symbols "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`sdk:WorkflowBuilderRootProps`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " and members "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`sdk:WorkflowBuilderRootProps.nodeTypes`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ".\n- Package READMEs are docs pages too: "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`readme/sdk`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`readme/ui`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`readme/temporal`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", and any other "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`.md`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " a package lists in "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`package.json`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`files`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " as "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`readme/<pkg>/<name>`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " (today "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`readme/ui/css-layers`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "; CHANGELOGs are left out). Sections use the same anchors as site pages, urls point at the file on GitHub and relative links are made absolute. They sit in a separate search index, and "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`readmeWeights`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " in "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`src/config/ranking.ts`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " scales their hits: the sdk and ui READMEs restate site pages, so they rank far below them, while the temporal README is the only place that documents installing the plugin and wiring a worker.\n- Components in "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`.mdx`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " are reduced to text by the rules in "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`src/config/mdx-components.ts`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ". Demo node schemas are not inlined; the page gets a pointer to the demo folder instead.\n- Temporal exports have no JSDoc, so they rank on name and signature.\n- A docs page that cannot be loaded (bad frontmatter, unclosed JSX, unknown "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`PropsTable`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " slug, missing partial, two files with one id) is skipped with one "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`wb-docs: skipped <file>: <reason>`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " line on stderr; the server keeps serving everything else. TypeDoc files that are empty or disagree with "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`manifest.json`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " also warn.\n- "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`build`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " runs TypeDoc twice per package: once for the entry points, and once over the files that declare types the package references without exporting ("
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`dist/data/typedoc/<package>.referenced.json`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "). "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`get_symbol`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " expands aliases of those types and serves them by name with "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`exported: false`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "; they are not searchable.\n- "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`<CssVariablesTable>`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " is rendered as one line of "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`--wb-public-*`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": " names read from "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`packages/ui/src/components/<dir>/**/*.css`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ". That line, link targets added after link text, the OverflowCard note, and list items that open with a link to another docs page ("
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`- [Next steps](/...)`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", also "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`*`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`+`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "`1.`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
